// securestore test root — `cpc test` discovers the `#[test]` fns in the modules
// this imports, and the imports are the point of the file.
//
// Same reason `vendor/http`, `vendor/permissions` and `vendor/notifications`
// have one: the facade deliberately does not import the backend — the two meet
// at stable symbols because the backend imports the facade for its types and a
// cycle back is rejected (E0404) — so a test driver built from the facade's own
// import graph would link against symbols nothing defined. It does not fail at
// discovery; it fails at `ld` with four undefined `__c_*`.

import "./securestore" as securestore;
import "./securestore_backend" as backend;
